WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:06.049
The Cancer Genome Project is an attempt to bring

00:00:06.049 --> 00:00:09.849
the human genome to the understanding of how cancers

00:00:09.849 --> 00:00:13.010
develop.

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:19.110
All our bodies are composed of cells.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:24.970
The human body has about 100 million million
cells within it,

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:27.500
and usually those cells behave in a very

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.949
ordered fashion.

00:00:30.949 --> 00:00:34.100
They observe certain rules, they

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.120
divide when they're told to divide, they're

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:41.170
quiescent when they're told to remain
quiescent, they stay in a particular

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:42.940
position within their tissue,

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:46.840
they don't move out of that.
Occasionally, however,

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:51.330
a single cell of those 100 million million
cells

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:54.379
decides to behave in a very different
way.

00:00:54.379 --> 00:00:59.260
That cell keeps on dividing

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:02.789
when all its signals around it tell it to
stop dividing.

00:01:02.789 --> 00:01:06.320
That cell ignores

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:09.840
its colleagues around it and pushes them
out of the way.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.869
That cell stops

00:01:12.869 --> 00:01:17.399
observing the rules of the tissue within which it is located

00:01:17.399 --> 00:01:21.160
and begins to move out of its normal
position,

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:25.100
invading into the tissues around it and
sometimes

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:29.549
entering the bloodstream and becoming
a metastasis,

00:01:29.549 --> 00:01:36.549
depositing in another tissue of the body.

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:38.820
The reason that the cell

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:43.520
behaves in this rogue fashion, is because it has acquired

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:47.250
within its genome, within its DNA,

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:53.550
a number of abnormalities that cause it to
behave as a cancer cell.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:57.040
Of course all these 100 million million
cells in the human body

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.600
have got a copy of the human genome, they've got two copies,

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.910
a maternal and paternal copy. And
throughout life

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:09.000
all those copies of the genome,

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.990
in those 100 million million cells, are
acquiring

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:17.370
abnormalities, so-called somatic
mutations.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.400
These are mutations that are just present in the cell, they're not

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:25.340
transmitted from parents to offspring,
they're just constrained to that individual

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:25.920
cell

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.930
and its progeny.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:31.460
And those mutations occur in every cell
of the body, normal

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:35.270
and abnormal, for a number of different
reasons. They occur

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:39.130
because although we have an
extraordinary mechanism

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:43.770
for replicating DNA, for those three
thousand million letters of code

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:48.930
to be replicated each time a cell divides,
hardly any mistakes are made,

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:52.980
despite that extraordinary mechanism,
the occasional mistake is made.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.280
Basically every time a cell divides

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:01.569
possibly one letter of code out of
the three thousand million is replicated

00:03:01.569 --> 00:03:02.090
wrongly.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:06.690
So that's one source of mistakes one
source of somatic mutations.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:10.849
However in addition to that, all these

00:03:10.849 --> 00:03:14.420
100 million million cells in the
body are being exposed to

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:18.040
a number of different onslaughts. There is
radiation,

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:22.209
of various sorts, which is hitting us the whole time, natural radiation;

00:03:22.209 --> 00:03:26.840
we are a bag of chemicals, chemicals that we generate ourselves,

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:31.200
but chemicals that we also ingest or are
exposed to,

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.940
and those also can bind

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:37.050
to DNA and can cause mistakes

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:44.050
in replication of DNA to be more common.

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:50.239
And finally, we have this mechanism,
these

00:03:50.239 --> 00:03:53.660
processes that allow DNA to be
replicated

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:56.959
in this highly faithful way, this high fidelity mode,

00:03:56.959 --> 00:04:01.520
but occasionally those mechanisms in a
particular cell may breakdown

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:05.260
and then the DNA of that cell begins to
acquire

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.480
mutations, somatic mutations rather more commonly

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.780
then other cells.

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:14.250
So, you put all that together, every cell
in the body

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:17.329
is acquiring mutations

00:04:17.329 --> 00:04:21.250
throughout a lifetime, and as we get older
we acquire more and more of them.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:25.090
As it turns out,

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:28.200
most of those mutations are

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:32.850
completely innocuous, they make no
difference at all. They make no difference to

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:33.880
the cell itself,

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:37.110
and certainly they make no difference to us as

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:41.360
multicellular organisms. They're basically
silent, they sit there,

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:44.880
we live with them.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:49.260
Occasionally, however, a mutation
takes place

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:52.890
in a particular type of gene, which

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:57.930
in an operative way we now call a
cancer gene. What that mutation

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:58.840
does

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:03.990
it changes that particular gene, and of
course the protein that it makes,

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:08.560
such that now that abnormal protein

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:11.650
is driving the cell to behave

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:15.510
in that unusual rogue fashion

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:17.130
that we call a cancer.

